      "content": "it's just that... the \"logic\" of it is what's killing me. in every other part of life, when an investment is totally dead and there's nothing left to salvage, you cut your losses and walk away. you don't keep throwing more time and more suffering into a void just for the sake of it. why is this any different? why is continuing the loss considered \"better\" than just ending the game?",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
